# GitHub accounts a mesh machine can push as. `mesh/build` turns this into
# ~/.ssh/config.d/github.conf, identical on every machine.
#
#   account  the GitHub login; `ssh -T` answers "Hi <account>!"
#   key      the key file in ~/.ssh — one per machine per account, made there
#            by `github-key-setup <account>` and never copied between boxes
#   git      the author a machine whose `github` column names this account
#            commits as, or - to leave git's identity alone
#   hosts    the ssh names that sign in as this account. The first line that
#            lists github.com is what plain git@github.com: remotes use.
#
# A second account is another line with its own alias (github.com-<account>)
# and its own key. A remote picks the account by the alias it is written with:
#   git@github.com-nerdnest:NerdNest-Engineering/levee.git
#
# account        | key                      | git                                  | hosts
felixflores      | id_dorkyrobot_ed25519    | Felix Flores <felix@dorkyrobot.com>  | github.com github.com-dorkyrobot
NerdNestFelix    | id_nerdnest_ed25519      | -                                    | github.com-nerdnest
